  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_5b984aab456d41238c1b1666739d277b",
      "statement": "Every RS485 topic-protocol frame is a single-line, CRLF-terminated, printable-ASCII JSON object carrying a type or cmd field plus a seq (u32) and ts (ms epoch), with an optional need_ack bool controlling whether the receiver must answer with an ACK.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://firmware/display/CLAUDE.md#L17-L21",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5889431c6bd4fa6a60b3cc1ee9602c3ba20bf7e081a520b2aacd02943e6223f6:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_2bab7e1fbb7b4ec59cb794f64d546592",
      "statement": "The documented ACK frame shape ({\"type\":\"ack\",\"ack\":<seq>,\"status\":\"ok\"|\"err\",...} in display/CLAUDE.md) differs from what the Sensorboard firmware actually sends ({\"type\":\"cmd_ack\",\"ack_seq\":<seq>,\"status\":\"ok\"|\"error\",...} in espnow_modem.c).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://firmware/display/CLAUDE.md#L21-L21",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6e74ac7643b08af26d0b4841273b6efd4574bea0dc149d60863db04cc4deec7c:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://firmware/sensorboard/main/network/espnow_modem.c#L260-L272",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:85229a3382ba188ded3d43ceecb8c1c8d92d7db9f63ef29dd004958f34936e99:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_2b73ca8918f9451092025630c2bb1718",
      "statement": "An incoming frame is treated as requiring an ACK whenever it carries a non-zero seq, even without an explicit need_ack:true; the explicit flag only overrides that default.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://firmware/sensorboard/main/network/espnow_modem.c#L1590-L1605",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d5db6634e22550ee0d4f3c23fdcc61b801e768f7c9c838698b2b4535a8643e2a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_a61d611bb7cf4add8b03903ee71b90b7",
      "statement": "The RS485 topic protocol's documented wired physical layer is half-duplex RS485 (MAX3485) at 57600 baud 8N1 with automatic DE/RTS toggling; 115200 baud was tried and abandoned because it caused UART framing errors from DE-toggle timing, making 57600 8N1 the correct, current value and 115200 a resolved historical pitfall.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://firmware/display/CLAUDE.md#L18-L18",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a83d4ab8e0676608e036748bf7af22243f23625f556e50c8bfd622cabc63f744:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://firmware/sensorboard/README.md#L19-L19",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bb721456a12adb8c00c46a17aec7a4377bdc79638c94cd4475240db15db1205c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_4410a2d3f24644988c74332829eb06e0",
      "statement": "sensorboard/README.md and display/CLAUDE.md disagree with each other on the Sensorboard's own RS485 pin numbers (TX=GPIO9/RX=GPIO10/DE=GPIO8 vs TX=GPIO12/RX=GPIO11/DE-RTS=GPIO21) for the same wired link.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://firmware/display/CLAUDE.md#L19-L19",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f78b69a5a1e86312840dec3811133501a9d1ee76dcd5f0648c0a8c7e7f23a823:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://firmware/sensorboard/README.md#L19-L19",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bb721456a12adb8c00c46a17aec7a4377bdc79638c94cd4475240db15db1205c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_781fb28797f24419a01850ff381a408c",
      "statement": "The RS485 topic protocol's JSON frames now run over an ESP-NOW transport rather than a wired UART bus: the Sensorboard's network/espnow_modem.c (internal functions still prefixed rs485_*, a naming holdover from the former rs485_modem.c) builds and parses every frame and sends/receives bytes via network/espnow_transport.c; the legacy RS485 UART pins are no longer driven as a UART, and sensorboard/README.md's project-structure section still names now-nonexistent network/rs485_modem and network/womo_rs485 modules.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://firmware/sensorboard/README.md#L164-L173",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e00ecb6f111a5aa9445faa0182686eb25df3e0d7db150b6743b759db6814a5a5:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://firmware/sensorboard/main/network/espnow_modem.c#L1-L50",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:69a68800128eb7d5e4024e89ff3c179a977bd16108e5a5713de1ff356bb81874:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://firmware/sensorboard/main/network/espnow_transport.c#L1-L50",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e8e0d1e8da6ba63e4c85f1fcdfaeb8dc1bbd6e5ad23790855693527e7151a434:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://firmware/sensorboard/main/sensor_config.h#L83-L87",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1eaca00345626348379085505fa1f07163de69dfe5058345824162593b5f3013:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_3b6b223110a740f6a22bb5e02ddf86f9",
      "statement": "Contrary to sensorboard/README.md and display/CLAUDE.md, which describe hello/hb as Sensorboard-to-Display heartbeat frames, the current espnow_modem.c only receives type:\"hb\"/\"hello\" frames (sent by the Display, per womo_config.h's WOMO_SENSOR_HEARTBEAT_INTERVAL_MS comment) and uses them purely as ESP-NOW peer-liveness signals, without the Sensorboard itself sending hello/hb.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://firmware/sensorboard/README.md#L41-L45",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c229080fbee7fa838cd03b23c2b86aa5d02a09dd1e90cc40acbf79ff94d179ec:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://firmware/sensorboard/main/network/espnow_modem.c#L1616-L1623",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5448b5b46088983df2e9945a72714ea91a2b1b1609f9e175bdd842556120b781:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://firmware/shared/womo_config.h#L29-L31",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:11dc2b058a540108d1777f56d68c9e305dc3c8f41f2a8f08048bca82bf554101:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_1a8863fdd6eb4e92861712443db500d2",
      "statement": "The Sensorboard's TX scheduler runs a 100 ms tick that publishes at most one due topic per tick in round-robin order across a fixed topic list (ctrl, imu, bat, tank, hx, gas, bme_in, bme_out, elec); on-demand frames (ruuvi_scan, gasbee_scan, gasbee_cal_result) consume the same one-frame-per-tick budget and temporarily displace regular topics.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://firmware/sensorboard/main/network/espnow_modem.c#L1387-L1399",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7becdc4b2af4b7e3fd52ebc61058b0df64ba71672afc17ce5f383c00f77d4c80:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://firmware/sensorboard/main/network/espnow_modem.c#L1656-L1729",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c2d267bc4a55f273b604cb1baad1319882c36163215f440ac04f8999f29ee050:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_26fb3d683a8448e8a1083a403a8af8ac",
      "statement": "The Sensorboard becomes 'ready' either on an explicit cmd:\"display_ready\" or as soon as the ESP-NOW transport recognizes the Display as a known peer, whichever happens first; becoming ready triggers a one-time initial burst publishing every topic back-to-back (~20 ms apart) before the interval-based round robin takes over.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://firmware/sensorboard/main/network/espnow_modem.c#L1669-L1676",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:19831814a109300762115e8aa64bbc1e24c3e16df8d88077602056ab6bd32e02:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://firmware/sensorboard/main/network/espnow_modem.c#L321-L347",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c782bcf6e38d8b46077115c710bbd2229ffd36ec6d14008516529f84c6c7a804:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_58a5ec7fea574b129c4994f46e09f374",
      "statement": "After executing pwr_12v_on/off or radio_on/off, the Sensorboard resets ctrl's interval timer and republishes ctrl immediately (s_ctrl_immediate) so the Display reflects the new state without waiting for ctrl's normal interval.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://firmware/display/CLAUDE.md#L36-L36",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:dab3d52316e0205f8e3d9634ab1580f051166710b2270dd0bb74ad63a0a3cea5:"
